 "preferred_name": "Ribosomal intergenic spacer analysis",
 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A DNA fingerprinting technique that compares the length of the spacer between two ribosomal RNA genes to profile the bacteria in a sample.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A method of analyzing microbial communities that compares environments or treatment effects without the bias of culture-dependent approaches. It uses PCR to amplify the intergenic spacer region of the rRNA gene operon between the 16S and 23S genes.",
